    <refnamediv>
        <refname>gf_is_prime</refname>
        <refpurpose>Tests whether integers are prime</refpurpose>
    </refnamediv>
    <refsynopsisdiv>
        <title>Syntax</title>
        <synopsis>tf = gf_is_prime(x)</synopsis>
    </refsynopsisdiv>
    <refsection>
        <title>Arguments</title>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>x</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Matrix of non-negative integers, smaller than 2^53.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>tf</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Boolean matrix of the same size as x: <literal>T</literal> where the entry is prime.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Description</title>
        <para><literal>gf_is_prime</literal> tests each entry of x by trial division. 0 and 1 are not prime. It can be used to check a characteristic before calling <link linkend="gf_create_field">gf_create_field</link>.</para>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Examples</title>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
gf_is_prime([0 1 2 9 97])      // [F F  T F T]
x = 1:30;
x(gf_is_prime(x))              // primes up to 30
]]></programlisting>
    </refsection>
